<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1721–1792</span> · Also known as Prince Ferdinand of Brunswick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a> was a Prussian field marshal and one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a>'s best generals. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> he commanded the allied army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> and Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1757, driving the French back across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and defeating them at Krefeld in 1758 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minden">Minden</a> in 1759.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-of-brunswick-wolfenbuttel.jpg" alt="Ferdinand of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joachim Martin Falbe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herzog_Ferdinand_von_Braunschweig_(Falbe%3F).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
